  "finalText": "Done. Here's what changed:\n\n**Problem:** `TaskService.create()` passed input directly to the repository with no title validation — empty/whitespace-only titles could reach the database if the service was called directly.\n\n**Fix — 2 files changed:**\n\n1. **`src/services/taskService.ts:9-14`** — Added defense-in-depth title validation at the service layer. Before calling the repository, `create()` now trims the title and throws `AppError('Title is required', 400)` if empty/missing. This runs before any database operation.\n\n2. **`tests/task.test.ts:56-72`** — Added two unit tests:\n   - Rejects empty string title with `AppError` / \"Title is required\", never calls repository\n   - Rejects whitespace-only title with `AppError` / \"Title is required\", never calls repository\n\n**Request path (now two defense layers):**\n```\nHTTP POST /api/tasks\n  → express-validator (route-level: 400) ← already existed\n  → TaskService.create() (service-level: 400) ← NEW\n  → TaskRepository.create() → DB\n```\n\n**Test results:** 234 total (231 passed, 3 pre-existing failures unrelated to tasks). All 35 task tests pass.",
